{"name":"Fair and Square","hex":"#8c9151","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fair and square","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Totally fairly and undoubtedly.","Within the applicable rules."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unquestionably fair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair_and_square"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fair & Square (John Prine album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fair & Square is the 15th studio album by American folk singer-songwriter John Prine, released on Oh Boy Records in 2005. It was rereleased in 2007 as a vinyl double-LP with four more bonus tracks, and in 2008 those four tracks were rereleased as an EP."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/Fair_and_Square_John_Prine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_%26_Square_(John_Prine_album)"},{"title":"Fair & Square (Jimmie Dale Gilmore album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fair & Square is the debut solo album by the American musician Jimmie Dale Gilmore, released in 1988. Gilmore supported the album with several live dates. The first single was \"Trying to Get to You\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/55/Fair_%26_Square_%28Jimmie_Dale_Gilmore_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_%26_Square_(Jimmie_Dale_Gilmore_album)"},{"title":"Fair and Square (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Fair and Square (1977–?) is a Filipino Thoroughbred racehorse and the first-ever Philracom Triple Crown champion (1981). He is also notable as the first horse to win back-to-back PCSO Presidential Gold Cup titles. As a sire, he produced Sun Dancer who won the Gold Cup two times in 1989 and 1990, and Fair Start who won the 1993 edition."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_and_Square_(horse)"},{"title":"Fair","blocks":[{"text":"A fair is gathering of people for a variety of entertainment or commercial activities. Fairs are typically temporary with scheduled times lasting from an afternoon to several weeks. Fairs showcase a wide range of goods, products, and services, and often include competitions, exhibitions, and educational activities. Fairs can be thematic, focusing on specific industries or interests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/2008Overview1.JPG/330px-2008Overview1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/1280px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy at the fish pond, the Rockton World's Fair, harvest festival, Canada, 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFairgames.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roundabouts (also known as a carousel or merry-go-round) are traditional attractions, often seen at fairs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG/500px-1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikiped